      :cards="[{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;UNEP-WCMC. (2021). Global relative rate of natural capital depletion of the atmosphere. Cambridge (UK): UNEP-WCMC. https://doi.org/10.34892/bjhg-8h63&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2023-05-05T12:50:04.982+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;-4712-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Global relative rate of natural capital depletion of the atmosphere, measured through t...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;58df19083c5c4b9e8c2083141ad162a6&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:162,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;Depletion of atmosphere was defined as emission of pollutants, which affects the delivery of ecosystem services such as climate regulation and air quality.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;natural-capital&quot;,&quot;atmospheric-conditions&quot;,&quot;depletion&quot;,&quot;cc-by&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global relative rate of natural capital depletion of the atmosphere&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2023-12-07T14:44:02.710+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/58df19083c5c4b9e8c2083141ad162a6/info/thumbnail/thumbnail.JPEG&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;UNEP-WCMC. (2002). Tree Cover in Mountain Regions. Cambridge (UK): UNEP-WCMC. https://doi.org/10.34892/dvwq-4j45&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-08T14:03:43.399+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2002-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The mountains dataset has been overlaid with a global data set on percent tree cover ta...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;7667394251834410a4708c8f619c4337&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:150,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:false,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;The mountains dataset has been overlayed with a global data set on percent tree cover taken from MODIS 1-km resolution percent tree cover data, courtesy of University of Maryland Global Land Cover Facility.\r\n\r\nMountain forests provide a range of services to mountain communities and to people outside mountain areas, and have a key role in the maintenance of global biodiversity. Species richness, density and forest height tend to reduce with increasing altitude; the boundary between forest vegetation and more open ground cover at higher elevation &#39;the treeline&#39; is an ecological marker signifying the transition to more extreme climatic conditions.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;Tree cover&quot;,&quot;Modis&quot;,&quot;global&quot;,&quot;dem&quot;,&quot;mountains&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Percent Tree Cover in Mountain Regions 2002&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2023-05-05T10:36:19.440+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/7667394251834410a4708c8f619c4337/info/thumbnail/tc_mtn_02g.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Murray N. J., Phinn S. R., DeWitt M., Ferrari R., Johnston R., Lyons M. B., Clinton N., Thau D. \u0026 Fuller R. A. (2019) The global distribution and trajectory of tidal flats. Nature. 565:222-225. http://dx.doi.org/10.1038/s41586-018-0805-8&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-10T12:41:33.138+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2019-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Download Dataset \n\nThe dataset contains global maps of tidal flat ecosystems produced v...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;498a5fe5db454f1f92342b14ceda1058&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:339,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;The dataset contains global maps of tidal flat ecosystems produced via a supervised classification of 707,528 Landsat Archive images. The maps were created to identify the non-vegetated areas of Earth&#39;s coastline that undergo regular tidal inundation. In some areas, these occur as tidal flats up to 24- km wide, such as the tidal mudflats of western Europe and East Asia. Our analysis included 56 predictor layers, many of which were Landsat composite metrics designed to identify individual pixels that undergo frequent wetting and drying.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;Intertidal Marsh&quot;,&quot;UNEP-WCMC&quot;,&quot;Ocean+ Habitats&quot;,&quot;landsat derived&quot;,&quot;uq&quot;,&quot;murray&quot;,&quot;tidal flats&quot;,&quot;intertidal&quot;,&quot;coastal&quot;,&quot;cc-by&quot;,&quot;ocean+&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global Distribution of Tidal Flat Ecosystems&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-05-28T11:20:44.597+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/498a5fe5db454f1f92342b14ceda1058/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1654865170704.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Pruckner, S., Thornton, H., McDermott-Long, O., De Lamo, X., Cugliari, L. \u0026 Gosling, J. 2021. Restoration Resilience: dataset. UNEP-WCMC. https://doi.org/10.34892/6v22-j032&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-08T14:03:46.809+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2021-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Restoration is a long-term process, and for it to be as efficient and effective as poss...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;77225ff9a7ed4b09a141fa0662426010&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:216,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;This layer shows a 2050 projection of how drastically climate change will affect restorable areas under a business-as-usual scenario. Areas with a low value have higher resilience, whereas areas with larger values are more vulnerable.\r\n\r\nRestoration is a long-term process, and for it to be as efficient and effective as possible, climate change impacts have to be considered before any action is carried out. This global screening layer of Restoration Resilience offers users a high-level overview of the climate resilience of restorable ecosystems. Different climate threats are considered, however, this is a global analysis that can only be used for scoping, screening and information gathering - before any action can take place, local, context- and species-specific research has to be conducted.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;unep-wcmc&quot;,&quot;restoration&quot;,&quot;cc-by&quot;,&quot;climate change&quot;,&quot;projections&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Restoration Resilience&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2023-05-31T09:46:06.623+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/77225ff9a7ed4b09a141fa0662426010/info/thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Kaschner K, Rius-Barile J, Kesner-Reyes K, Garilao C, Kullander SO, Rees T, Froese R (2013). AquaMaps: Predicted range maps for aquatic species. World wide web electronic publication: www.aquamaps.org, Version August 2013&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-17T10:37:16.570+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2013-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Access latest version \n\nThis dataset shows the modelled distribution of Northern fur se...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;b321df335f714c129986ce546cf76c25&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by-nc&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:165,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;This dataset shows the modelled distribution of Northern fur seals (Callorhinus ursinus). AquaMaps is a tool for generating model-based, large-scale predictions of natural occurrences of species. The maps can be used to inform environmental impact assessments.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;marine&quot;,&quot;coastal&quot;,&quot;model&quot;,&quot;high seas&quot;,&quot;pelagic&quot;,&quot;cc-by-nc&quot;,&quot;ocean+&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global Distribution of Northern Fur Seals (2013)&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-05-28T11:03:37.912+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/b321df335f714c129986ce546cf76c25/info/thumbnail/thumbnail.JPEG&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Original Natural Habitats of the Indo-Malayan Realm produced in collaboration with The\nAsian Bureau for Conservation (ABC) for the publication \&quot;Protected Areas Systems Review of the IndoMalayan Realm, Mackinnon, J. ed. 1997.&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-08-03T13:16:23.761+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;1997-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;This dataset was created show the original habitat types as they were before man&#39;s infl...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;46ae1fdf664e482088985008f4e9275b&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:406,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?