ectra).  AquaMaps is a tool for generating model-based, large-scale predictions of natural occurrences of species. The maps can be used to inform environmental impact assessments.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;marine&quot;,&quot;coastal&quot;,&quot;model&quot;,&quot;pelagic&quot;,&quot;high seas&quot;,&quot;deep sea&quot;,&quot;cc-by-nc&quot;,&quot;ocean+&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global Distribution of Melon-Headed Whales (2013)&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-05-28T10:58:38.845+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/36c329918fb344bbb0a3bf7529d8a1d1/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1655461842873.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;UNEP-WCMC (1999). Global distribution of sea turtle feeding sites (version 1.1). Cambridge (UK): UN Environment Programme World\nConservation Monitoring Centre. Data DOI:\nhttps://doi.org/10.34892/4eza-0021&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-15T16:03:38.838+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;-4712-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Download Dataset \n\n\nThis dataset shows the known locations of sea turtle feeding sites,...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;4f0eccd159a643e6a2a2000f64d12715&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:242,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;This is a legacy dataset showing the known locations of sea turtle feeding sites, for five of the seven species: hawksbill turtle (Eretmochelys imbricata), leatherback turtle (Dermochelys coriacea), green turtle (Chelonia mydas), loggerhead turtle (Caretta caretta), and olive ridley turtle (Lepidochelys olivacea). The dataset is the only global source of sea turtle feeding sites.&quot;,&quot;ta