vation Union between 1994 and 1997&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-08T14:03:16.005+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;-4712-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;This dataset provides spatial representation for the 234 “Data Sheet Sites” in the Cent...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;ddd809db3edc4945a100af6ccec703d8&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:998,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:false,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;This dataset has been digitized to give a spatial representation of the Centres of Plant Diversity (hereafter “CPDs”) presented in the three-volume work “Centres of Plant Diversity”, edited by S.D. Davis, V.H. Heywood and A.C. Hamilton, and published by the World Wildlife Fund for Nature (WWF) and IUCN – The World Conservation Union between 1994 and 1997.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;cpd&quot;,&quot;plants&quot;,&quot;diversity&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Centres of Plant Diversity&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-09-19T16:06:34.554+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/ddd809db3edc4945a100af6ccec703d8/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1664807549270.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Kaschner K, Rius-Barile J, Kesner-Reyes K, Garilao C, Kullander SO, Rees T, Froese R (2013). AquaMaps: Predicted range maps for aquatic species. World wide web electronic publication: www.aquamaps.org, Version August 2013&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-16T10:34:58.973+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2013-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Access latest version \nThis dataset shows the modelled distribution of grey seals (Hali...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;d5fb746a6beb4774b846a75de6967f2f&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by-nc&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:227,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;This dataset shows the modelled distribution of grey seals (Halichoerus grypus). AquaMaps is a tool for generating model-based, large-scale predictions of natural occurrences of species. The maps can be used to inform environmental impact assessments.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;marine&quot;,&quot;coastal&quot;,&quot;model&quot;,&quot;high seas&quot;,&quot;pelagic&quot;,&quot;cc-by-nc&quot;,&quot;ocean+&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global Distribution of Grey Seals&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-05-28T12:03:40.962+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/d5fb746a6beb4774b846a75de6967f2f/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1655376224346.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;UNEP-WCMC and IUCN (2025), Protected Planet: The World Database on Protected Areas (WDPA)[On-line], [October 2025], Cambridge, UK: UNEP-WCMC and IUCN. Available at: https://doi.org/10.34892/6fwd-af11&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-08T14:04:32.660+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;-4712-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;\n                                The World Database of Protected Areas (WDPA) is the mo...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;693072da735e4850acb0c0fceb1db99b&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;wdpa&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:1499,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;The World Database on Protected Areas (WDPA) is the most comprehensive global database on terrestrial and marine protected areas. Version: October 2025. &quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;wdpa&quot;,&quot;protected-planet&quot;,&quot;wdpa&quot;,&quot;protected-areas&quot;,&quot;areas-of-biodiversity-importance&quot;,&quot;Proteus&quot;,&quot;Proteus Partners&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;The World Database of Protected Areas Licensed&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2025-10-01T14:25:05.748+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/693072da735e4850acb0c0fceb1db99b/info/thumbnail/thumbnail.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Gosling, J., Jones, M. I., Arnell, A., Venter, O., Watson, J. E. M., Baquero, A. C., \u0026 Burgess, N. D. (2020). Natural and Modified Habitat Screening Layer [Data set]. UN Environment Programme World Conservation Monitoring Centre (UNEP-WCMC). https://doi.org/10.34892/4Q5V-GF37&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-08T14:03:09.927+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2020-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;This dataset uses a combination of freely available data layers to develop a new global...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;4e2d929b580b40f48513906ca5097140&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:2076,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;This dataset classifies the global terrestrial land surface into one of four categories: likely Natural, potential Natural, potential Modified, and likely Modified.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;unep-wcmc&quot;,&quot;international-finance-corporation-performance-standard-6&quot;,&quot;biodiversity-safeguards&quot;,&quot;natural-habitat&quot;,&quot;modified-habitat&quot;,&quot;investment-screening&quot;,&quot;environmental-risk&quot;,&quot;cc-by&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Natural and Modified Habitat Screening Layer&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-05-07T21:02:27.877+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/4e2d929b580b40f48513906ca5097140/info/thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Burke L, Reytar K, Spalding M and Perry A (2011). Reefs At Risk Revisited. Washington (USA): World Resources Institute. 130 pp. URL: http://www.wri.org/publication/reefs-risk-revisited.&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-15T14:49:06.391+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2011-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Download Dataset \n\nThe Reefs at Risk Revisited report provides a detailed assessment of...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;4b411a9709ea4b0da4ad97a6e19a48e0&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:719,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;Reefs at Risk Revisited (2011) is a high-resolution update of the original global analysis, Reefs at Risk: A Map-Based Indicator of Threats to the World’s Coral Reefs, 1998. Reefs at Risk Revisited (2011) is a high-resolution update of the original global analysis, Reefs at Risk: A Map-Based Indicator of Threats to the World’s Coral Reefs, 1998. Reefs at Risk Revisited uses a global map of coral reefs at 500-m resolution, which is 64 times more detailed than the 4-km resolution map used in the 1998 analysis, and benefits from improvements in many global data sets used to evaluate threats to reefs (most threat data are at 1 km resolution, which is 16 times more detailed than those used in the 1998 analysis).&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;coral reefs&quot;,&quot;climate change&quot;,&quot;ecosystem services&quot;,&quot;fisheries&quot;,&quot;oceans&quot;,&quot;water&quot;,&quot;cc-by&quot;,&quot;ocean+&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Reefs at Risk Revisited&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-05-28T11:29:16.538+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/4b411a9709ea4b0da4ad97a6e19a48e0/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1655307233313.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Kaschner K, Rius-Barile J, Kesner-Reyes K, Garilao C, Kullander SO, Rees T, Froese R (2013). AquaMaps: Predicted range maps for aquatic species. World wide web electronic publication: www.aquamaps.org, Version August 2013&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-17T10:17:15.555+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2013-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Access latest version \nThis dataset shows the modelled distribution of Northern bottlen...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;3033d6e8c477450681afffc770402cce&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by-nc&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:186,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;This dataset shows the modelled distribution of Northern bottlenose whales (Hyperoodon ampullatus). AquaMaps is a tool for generating model-based, large-scale predictions of natural\r\noccurrences of species. The maps can be used to inform environmental impact\r\nassessments.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;marine&quot;,&quot;coastal&quot;,&quot;model&quot;,&quot;pelagic&quot;,&quot;high seas&quot;,&quot;cc-by-nc&quot;,&quot;ocean+&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global Distribution of Northern Bottlenose Whales (2013)&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-05-28T11:03:00.602+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/3033d6e8c477450681afffc770402cce/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1655461600435.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Citation: \n\nLeemans, R. (1992). Global Holdridge Life Zone Classifications. Laxenberg (Austria): IIASA.&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-08T14:03:08.734+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;1990-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Holdridge’s work was aimed to correlate world plant formations with simple climatic dat...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;746658218d974db3a094a2c05ae0b798&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:485,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:false,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;Map of Holdridge&#39;s life zone system&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;Holdridge&quot;,&quot;Life Zones&quot;,&quot;global&quot;,&quot;world&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Holdridge&#39;s Life Zones (1992)&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-23T14:43:39.151+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/746658218d974db3a094a2c05ae0b798/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1655995419069.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Dunn, D. C., A.-L. Harrison, C. Curtice, S. DeLand, B. Donnelly, E. Fujioka, E. Heywood, C. Y. Kot, S. Poulin, M. Whitten, S. Åkesson, A. Alberini, W. Appeltans, J. M. Arcos, H. Bailey, L. T. Ballance, B. Block, H. Blondin, A. M. Boustany, J. Brenner, P. Catry, D. Cejudo, J. Cleary, P. Corkeron, D. P. Costa, M. Coyne, G. O. Crespo, T. E. Davies, M. P. Dias, F. Douvere, F. Ferretti, A. Formia, D. Freestone, A. S. Friedlaender, H. Frisch-Nwakanma, C. B. Froján, K. M. Gjerde, L. Glowka, B. J. Godley, J. Gonzalez-Solis, J. P. Granadeiro, V. Gunn, Y. Hashimoto, L. M. Hawkes, G. C. Hays, C. Hazin, J. Jimenez, D. E. Johnson, P. Luschi, S. M. Maxwell, C. McClellan, M. Modest, G. Notarbartolo di Sciara, A. H. Palacio, D. M. Palacios, A. Pauly, M. Rayner, A. F. Rees, E. R. Salazar, D. Secor, A. M. M. Sequeira, M. Spalding, F. Spina, S. Van Parijs, B. Wallace, N. Varo-Cruz, M. Virtue, H. Weimerskirch, L. Wilson, B. Woodward, and P. N. Halpin. 2019. The importance of migratory connectivity for global ocean policy. Proceedings of the Royal Society B: Biological Sciences 286:20191472. Available from the MiCO System Version 1.0. MiCO. https://mico.eco.&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-17T13:34:32.441+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2019-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Advancements in animal tracking technology are enabling far greater data collection on ...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;70f106bb2e9049669b92ee26932055c2&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:1420,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;An objective of the Migratory Connectivity in the Ocean (MiCO) initiative is to synthesize data on marine migratory species area use to support worldwide conservation efforts.  These general areas of use are further partitioned into MiCO nodes which are aggregated areas of non-migratory behavior (e.g., wintering, breeding, foraging), and MiCO corridors which are aggregated areas used by migrating individuals. Nodes and corridors are generated using animal tracking data via well-accepted kernel density estimation (KDE) methods using R statistical software (R Core Team 2018).&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;areas beyond national jurisdiction&quot;,&quot;migratory species&quot;,&quot;marine spatial planning&quot;,&quot;area-based management&quot;,&quot;cc-by&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Migratory Connectivity in the Ocean (MiCO)&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2023-01-24T16:01:48.840+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/70f106bb2e9049669b92ee26932055c2/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1655473049701.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Kaschner K, Rius-Barile J, Kesner-Reyes K, Garilao C, Kullander SO, Rees T, Froese R (2013). AquaMaps: Predicted range maps for aquatic species. World wide web electronic publication: www.aquamaps.org, Version August 2013&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-17T12:12:23.181+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2013-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Access latest version \n\nThis dataset shows the modelled distribution of sperm whales (P...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;35dd52a5d227468a98db781b6437966e&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by-nc&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:448,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;This dataset shows the modelled distribution of sperm whales (Physeter macrocephalus). AquaMaps version used: 01 August 2013. In acknowledgement that predicted distributions reflect the current state of knowledge, AquaMaps predictions are not a permanent, fixed output, but instead will be revised and updated as new data or information become available or additional experts provide new input.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;marine&quot;,&quot;coastal&quot;,&quot;model&quot;,&quot;pelagic&quot;,&quot;high seas&quot;,&quot;deep sea&quot;,&quot;cc-by-nc&quot;,&quot;ocean+&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global Distribution of Sperm Whales (2013)&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-05-28T11:14:24.451+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/35dd52a5d227468a98db781b6437966e/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1655468282635.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;UNEP-WCMC. (2000). Mountains of the World. Cambridge (UK): UNEP-WCMC. https://doi.org/10.34892/jh4m-0h26&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-08T14:03:14.543+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2000-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;To produce this map, topographical data from the GTOPO30 global digital elevation model...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;e6862c0331d04362ab7dc5bae983c5f6&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:620,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:false,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;To provide a global context for a discussion of mountain forests, it is first necessary to define the locations and types of mountain forests, and this in turn requires a definition of mountains or mountain areas. Altitude and slope and the environmental gradients they generate are key components of such a definition, but their combination is problematic. Simple altitude thresholds both exclude older and lower mountain systems and include areas of relatively high elevation that have little topographic relief and few environmental gradients. Using slope as a criterion on its own or in combination with altitude can resolve the latter problem, but not the former.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;mountains&quot;,&quot;global&quot;,&quot;dem&quot;,&quot;gtopo30&quot;,&quot;elevation&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Mountains of the World - 2000&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-23T14:53:48.957+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/e6862c0331d04362ab7dc5bae983c5f6/info/thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Aldrich, M., Billington, C., Edwards, M., Laidlaw, R. (1997). Locations of tropical montane cloud forest sites as recorded in a worldwide inventory in \&quot;A Global Directory of Tropical Montane Cloud Forests\&quot;. Cambridge (UK): UNEP-WCMC.&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-08T14:03:16.093+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;1997-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Download Dataset This dataset shows the location of tropical montane cloud forest sites...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;764b2ceab8304729a7a162cc1a0dbc95&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:770,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:false,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;Tropical montane cloud forests represent a rare and fragile ecosystem that is under threat in many parts of the world. Urgent action is needed to conserve these rich mountain forests, not only because they harbour concentrations of endemic and threatened species but to maintain their vital role in the provision of freshwater. All tropical forests are under threat but cloud forests are uniquely threatened both by human pressures and by climate change impacting on temperature, rainfall and the formation of clouds in mountain areas. Cloud forests are a rare habitat of tropical mountains which have not received sufficient attention for their exceptional concentrations of biodiversity and as sources of freshwater. This threat and rarity makes it necessary to map the location of cloud forests to improve understanding and conservation efforts.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;cloud&quot;,&quot;forest&quot;,&quot;cloud forests&quot;,&quot;forests&quot;,&quot;tropical&quot;,&quot;montane&quot;,&quot;mountain&quot;,&quot;global&quot;,&quot;world&quot;,&quot;Africa&quot;,&quot;Americas&quot;,&quot;Asia&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Tropical Montane Cloud Forest Sites 1997&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-06-07T11:56:33.818+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/764b2ceab8304729a7a162cc1a0dbc95/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1655995096860.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Yesson C, Clark MR, Taylor M, Rogers AD (2011). The global distribution of seamounts based on 30-second bathymetry data. Deep Sea Research Part I: Oceanographic Research Papers 58: 442-453. DOI: http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.dsr.2011.02.004. Data DOI: http://doi.pangaea.de/10.1594/PANGAEA.757564.&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-10T10:44:05.367+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2011-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Download Dataset \n\nThis dataset shows the global distribution of seamounts and knolls i...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;4490b872250548a79e8c96da199be5f4&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:1939,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;This dataset shows the global distribution of seamounts and knolls identified using global bathymetric data at 30 arc-sec resolution.\r\n\r\nSeamounts and knolls provide important habitats for marine predators, demersal  deep-sea fish and benthic invertebrates. Most seamounts, however, have not been  surveyed and their numbers and locations are not well known. Previous efforts to  locate and quantify seamounts have used relatively coarse bathymetry grids. \r\n\r\nThe database of seamounts and knolls resulting from this study will be a useful resource for researchers and conservation planners.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;zsl&quot;,&quot;deep sea&quot;,&quot;high seas&quot;,&quot;benthic&quot;,&quot;marine&quot;,&quot;model&quot;,&quot;seamount&quot;,&quot;knoll&quot;,&quot;habitat&quot;,&quot;ecosystem&quot;,&quot;cc-by&quot;,&quot;ocean+&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global Distribution of Seamounts and Knolls (2011)&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-05-28T11:12:14.615+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/4490b872250548a79e8c96da199be5f4/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1655973111171.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Freiwald A, Rogers A, Hall-Spencer J, Guinotte JM, Davies AJ, Yesson C, Martin CS, Weatherdon LV (2021). Global distribution of cold-water corals (version 5.1). Fifth update to the dataset in Freiwald et al. (2004) by UNEP-WCMC, in collaboration with Andre Freiwald and John Guinotte. Cambridge (UK): UN Environment Programme World Conservation Monitoring Centre. Data DOI: https://doi.org/10.34892/72x9-rt61&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-08T14:03:55.444+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2004-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Download Dataset \nThis dataset shows of the global distribution of cold-water corals. O...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;fb9b160602e84a139ffc4fc16cf74bfc&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:3480,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;This dataset shows of the known global distribution of cold-water corals, with occurrence records for 86 families.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;deep sea&quot;,&quot;high seas&quot;,&quot;benthic&quot;,&quot;marine&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;ocean+&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global Distribution of Cold-Water Corals&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-05-28T12:05:10.158+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/fb9b160602e84a139ffc4fc16cf74bfc/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1655992185918.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Citation: \n\nLeemans, R. (1992). Global Holdridge Life Zone Classifications. Laxenberg (Austria): IIASA.&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-08T14:03:15.980+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;1990-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Holdridge’s work was aimed to correlate world plant formations with simple climatic dat...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;31d5e80482834f6ba6ee51a2813b82e7&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:2572,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:false,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;Map of Holdridge&#39;s life zone system&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;Holdridge&quot;,&quot;Life Zones&quot;,&quot;global&quot;,&quot;world&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Holdridge&#39;s Life Zones (1992)&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-23T14:42:30.223+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/31d5e80482834f6ba6ee51a2813b82e7/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1655995350146.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Ramirez-Llodra, E., Blanco, M. and Arcas, A., (2004). Cold Seeps. ChEssBase: an online information system on biodiversity and biogeography of deep-sea chemosynthetic ecosystems. Version 1. World Wide Web electronic publications, www.noc.soton.ac.uk/chess/db_home.php.&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-09T11:15:43.600+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2010-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The main aim of ChEss is to determine the biogeography of deep-water chemosynthetic eco...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;c93a5c2629cc4ed0bba3520d6d288657&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;bespoke&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:804,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;Only a small fraction of the global ridge system (approx. 65,000 km) and of the vast  continental margin regions have been explored and their communities described.  \nThe ChEss project aimed to improve knowledge on the diversity, abundance and distribution of species from vents, seeps and other reducing habitats at a global  scale, to understand the abiotic and biotic processes that shape and maintan these ecosystems and their biogeography. The field programme aimed to explain the main gaps in our knowledge of the diversity, abundance and distribution of \nchemosynthetic species globally.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;cold seeps&quot;,&quot;cold&quot;,&quot;seeps&quot;,&quot;chess&quot;,&quot;marine&quot;,&quot;biogeography&quot;,&quot;deep&quot;,&quot;deep-sea&quot;,&quot;bespoke&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global Distribution of Cold Seeps (2010)&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2023-12-15T09:53:25.014+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/c93a5c2629cc4ed0bba3520d6d288657/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1677076144809.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Miles, L., Newton, A.C., DeFries, R.S., Ravilious, C., May, I., Blyth, S., Kapos, V., Gordon, J.E. (2006). A global overview of the conservation status of tropical dry forests. Journal of Biogeography. 33(3): 491-505. https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-2699.2005.01424.x&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-08T14:03:45.228+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2006-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Download Dataset  The global biogeographic classification presented by Olson et al. (20...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;2e98ecf8077347a2a1587b36cdfda220&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:520,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:false,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;Global distribution of tropical dry forest in the year 2000 (this includes but does not distinguish between plantations in tropical dry forest areas). Based on biogeographic realms from Olson et al. (2001) masked with MODIS 500-m resolution forest cover data set (Hansen et al., 2003), with forest canopy cover greater than 40%.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;tropical&quot;,&quot;dry&quot;,&quot;forest&quot;,&quot;tropical dry forest&quot;,&quot;global&quot;,&quot;world&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc&quot;,&quot;tdf&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global tropical dry forest&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-06-07T10:01:41.610+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/2e98ecf8077347a2a1587b36cdfda220/info/thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;UNEP-WCMC. (2002). Mountains of the World. Cambridge (UK): UNEP-WCMC. https://doi.org/10.34892/4wep-p033&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-08T14:03:09.932+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2002-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;To provide a global context for a discussion of mountain forests, it is first necessary...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;9613e454c5b54b2b85627ca6c8a658d5&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:748,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:false,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;Shows the location of mountain land estimated from a digital elevation model using criteria based on elevation alone (upper three classes: greater 2 500 metres) and at lower elevation, on a combination of elevation, slope and local elevation range.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;mountains&quot;,&quot;elevation&quot;,&quot;global&quot;,&quot;dem&quot;,&quot;mountain-watch&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Mountains of the World - 2002&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-23T14:55:39.053+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/9613e454c5b54b2b85627ca6c8a658d5/info/thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;UNEP-WCMC and IUCN (2025), Protected Planet: The World Database on other effective area-based conservation measures(WD-OECM)[On-line], [October 2025], Cambridge, UK: UNEP-WCMC and IUCN. Available at: https://doi.org/10.34892/ndcc-cs86&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-16T12:27:21.280+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;-4712-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;\n                                \n                                In 2018, the governme...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;4c1733823f2a451e8d5ecbaaef3f1a06&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;wdpa&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:3381,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:false,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;Other Effective Area-based Conservation Measures (OECMs) complement protected areas through sustained, positive conservation outcomes, even though they may be managed primarily for other reasons. Version: October 2025.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;wdpa&quot;,&quot;protected-planet&quot;,&quot;wdpa&quot;,&quot;protected-areas&quot;,&quot;areas-of-biodiversity-importance&quot;,&quot;other-effective-area-based-conservation-measures&quot;,&quot;oecms&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;The World Database on other effective area based conservation measures&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2025-10-01T14:25:03.049+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/4c1733823f2a451e8d5ecbaaef3f1a06/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1743774684444.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;UNEP-WCMC (1999). Global distribution of sea turtle nesting sites (ver 1.1). Cambridge (UK): UNEP World Conservation Monitoring Centre. Data DOI: https://doi.org/10.34892/1731-mc59 URL: http://data.unep-wcmc.org/datasets/22&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-16T08:08:12.528+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;1999-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Download Dataset \n\n\nThis dataset shows the known locations of sea turtle nesting sites,...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;0e037e25683a4b3182f1e4697f2e6666&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:841,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;This is a legacy dataset of the global distribution of sea turtle nesting sites (version 1.1, updated by UNEP-WCMC). At the time of compilation, the dataset was the only global source of sea turtle nesting sites.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;unep-wcmc&quot;,&quot;coastal&quot;,&quot;marine&quot;,&quot;turtle&quot;,&quot;habitat&quot;,&quot;IUCN&quot;,&quot;threatened&quot;,&quot;nesting&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;ocean+&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global Distribution of Sea Turtle Nesting Sites&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-06-07T18:03:47.182+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/0e037e25683a4b3182f1e4697f2e6666/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1655367397396.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Mcowen C, Weatherdon LV, Bochove J, Sullivan E, Blyth S, Zockler C, Stanwell-Smith D, Kingston N, Martin CS, Spalding M, Fletcher S (2017). A global map of saltmarshes (v6.1). Biodiversity Data Journal 5: e11764. Paper DOI: https://doi.org/10.3897/BDJ.5.e11764 ; Data DOI: https://doi.org/10.34892/07vk-ws51&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-08T14:03:56.410+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2021-03-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Download Dataset \n\n\nThis dataset displays the extent of our knowledge regarding the dis...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;addd1baa160c4d318b84c3b714d3e583&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by-nc&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:5290,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;This dataset displays the extent of our knowledge regarding the distribution of saltmarshes globally, drawing from occurrence data (surveyed and/or remotely sensed).&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;global&quot;,&quot;saltmarshes&quot;,&quot;intertidal&quot;,&quot;cc-by-nc&quot;,&quot;ocean+&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global Distribution of Saltmarshes&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-05-28T11:05:37.928+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/addd1baa160c4d318b84c3b714d3e583/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1655992958498.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Worthington, T.A., zu Ermgassen, P.S.E., Friess, D.A., Krauss, K.W., Lovelock, C.E., Thorley, J., Tingey, R., Woodroffe, C.D., Bunting, P., Cormier, N., Lagomasino, D., Lucas, R., Murray, N.J., Sutherland, W.J., Spalding, M., 2020. A global biophysical typology of mangroves and its relevance for ecosystem structure and deforestation. Sci. Rep. 10, 14652. https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-71194-5&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2024-04-17T09:57:58.740+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2020-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Download Dataset \n\nThe dataset contains five layers. One each for the 1996, 2007, 2010 ...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;6688fafdbbd84b59850cdf07c406cf24&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:1851,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:false,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;The typology classifies the mangroves of the world based on their geomorphic and sedimentary setting. The typology also divides the global mangrove extent into 4,318 macroscale units.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;coastal&quot;,&quot;mangrove&quot;,&quot;geomorphic&quot;,&quot;typology&quot;,&quot;sedimentary&quot;,&quot;cc-by&quot;,&quot;ocean+&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;A global biophysical typology of mangroves&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-05-28T12:27:03.389+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/6688fafdbbd84b59850cdf07c406cf24/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1713356736908.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Bunting P., Rosenqvist A., Lucas R., Rebelo L-M., Hilarides L., Thomas N., Hardy A., Itoh T., Shimada M. and Finlayson C.M. (2018). The Global Mangrove Watch – a New 2010 Global Baseline of Mangrove Extent. Remote Sensing 10(10): 1669. doi: 10.3390/rs1010669&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-07-01T15:20:24.165+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;-4712-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Download Dataset \n\n\nThe Global Mangrove Watch (GMW) was initiated as part of the JAXA K...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;5e72c1881c524cd4bd0ca28a809514a2&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:35138,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;The GMW has generated a global baseline map of mangroves for 2010 using ALOS PALSAR and Landsat (optical) data, and changes from this baseline for epochs between 1996 and 2020 derived from JERS-1 SAR, ALOS PALSAR and ALOS-2 PALSAR-2. Annual maps are planned from 2015 and onwards.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;coastal&quot;,&quot;blue carbon&quot;,&quot;remote sensing&quot;,&quot;satellite&quot;,&quot;mangrove&quot;,&quot;forest&quot;,&quot;habitat&quot;,&quot;ecosystem&quot;,&quot;cc-by&quot;,&quot;ocean+&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global Mangrove Watch&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-05-28T11:20:25.805+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/5e72c1881c524cd4bd0ca28a809514a2/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1659425921071.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Citation:\nUNEP-WCMC. (1998). Global Generalised Original and Current Forest Cover dataset (V 3.0). Cambridge (UK): UNEP-WCMC.&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-08T14:03:15.749+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;1998-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;This dataset, compiled from various sources at UNEP-WCMC, shows the current extent of g...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;e56277812f854e7ca8fa9282ee323c5e&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:7099,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:false,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;About half of the forest that was present under modern (i.e. post-Pleistocene) climatic conditions, and before the spread of human influence, has disappeared, largely through the impact of man&#39;s activities. The spread of agriculture and animal husbandry, the harvesting of forests for timber and fuel, and the expansion of populated areas have all taken their toll on forests. The causes and timing of forest loss differ between regions and forest types, as do the current trends in change in forest cover.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;current forest cover&quot;,&quot;current&quot;,&quot;forest&quot;,&quot;cover&quot;,&quot;needle-leaf&quot;,&quot;temperate&quot;,&quot;broadleaf&quot;,&quot;tropical dry&quot;,&quot;tropical moist&quot;,&quot;tropical&quot;,&quot;UNEP-WCMC&quot;,&quot;global&quot;,&quot;world&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global Generalised &#39;Original&#39; and &#39;Current&#39; Forest&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-23T14:31:00.655+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/e56277812f854e7ca8fa9282ee323c5e/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1655994660575.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Full citation:\n\nUNEP-WCMC. (2007). A spatial analysis approach to the global delineation of dryland areas of relevance to the CBD Programme of Work on Dry and Subhumid Lands. Dataset based on spatial analysis between WWF terrestrial ecoregions (WWF-US, 2004) and aridity zones (CRU/UEA; UNEPGRID, 1991). Dataset checked and refined to remove many gaps, overlaps and slivers (July 2014). Cambridge (UK): UNEP-WCMC.\n\nReferences:\n\nMiles, L., A.C. Newton, R.S. DeFries, C. Ravilious, I. May, S. Blyth, V. Kapos and J.E. Gordon.  (2006).  A global overview of the conservation status of tropical dry forests. J. Biogeogr. 33: 491–505.                                                                                             \n\nSorensen, L. (2007).  A spatial analysis approach to the global delineation of dryland areas of relevance to the CBD Programme of Work on Dry and Subhumid Lands.  UNEP-WCMC, Cambridge.\n&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-23T14:25:00.606+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2007-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Download dataset The original dataset developed by the MA is a subset of the aridity zo...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;789fcac8959943ab9ed7a225e5316f08&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:6320,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:false,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;The original drylands dataset was developed to define the Millennium Ecosystem Assessment (MA) dryland system boundary. Sörensen (2007) used this map to further delineate dryland areas of relevance to the CBD Programme of Work on Dry and Subhumid Lands. This current dataset builds on these maps to incorporate additional features to update the data to better reflect dry and sub-humid tropical forests in accordance with paragraph 13 of  Convention on Biological Diversity (CBD) CoP Decision IX/17.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;hyperarid&quot;,&quot;semiarid&quot;,&quot;dryland&quot;,&quot;dryland ecosystem&quot;,&quot;Condition and Trends&quot;,&quot;arid&quot;,&quot;dry subhumid&quot;,&quot;aridity index&quot;,&quot;global&quot;,&quot;MA system&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;World Dryland Areas&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2025-03-12T14:57:12.638+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/789fcac8959943ab9ed7a225e5316f08/info/thumbnail/thumbnail.JPEG&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Udvardy, M. D. F. (1975). A classification of the biogeographical provinces of the world. IUCN Occasional Paper no. 18. Morges (Switzerland): IUCN \u0026 \&quot;World Biogeographical Provinces\&quot; (Map). The CoEvolution Quarterly, Sausalito, California.&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-08T14:03:52.552+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;1975-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Udvardy&#39;s map of biogeographical provinces.\r\n\r\nThere are three versions of the dataset ...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;7f3a055f36104f36b6dd7834ebe2cf45&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:2172,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:false,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;This map was prepared by IUCN as a contribution to the UNESCO MAB Programme. The main purpose of the work was to devise a satisfactory classification of the world&#39;s biotic areas for purposes of conservation. It is the fourth attempt in a series of revisions, updating the previous three works written by Dasmann.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;Udvardy&quot;,&quot;Biogeographic&quot;,&quot;Biome&quot;,&quot;Realm&quot;,&quot;global&quot;,&quot;world&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Udvardy&#39;s Biogeographical Provinces (1975)&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-23T15:08:57.289+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/7f3a055f36104f36b6dd7834ebe2cf45/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1655996937205.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;The Nature Conservancy (2012). Marine Ecoregions and Pelagic Provinces of the World. GIS layers developed by The Nature Conservancy with multiple partners, combined from Spalding et al. (2007) and Spalding et al. (2012). Cambridge (UK): The Nature Conservancy. DOIs: 10.1641/B570707; 10.1016/j.ocecoaman.2011.12.016.&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-15T14:24:44.802+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2017-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Download Dataset \n\n\nThis dataset combines two separately published datasets: the  “Mari...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;80567b4443f4457b822f645a2f0d70cf&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:2003,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;This dataset was developed to address the need for a detailed, biogeographic system to classify the oceans. It provides better spatial resolution than earlier global systems, but may also be cross-referenced to many regional biogeographic classifications.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;MEOW&quot;,&quot;PPOW&quot;,&quot;UNEP-WCMC&quot;,&quot;marine&quot;,&quot;coastal&quot;,&quot;high seas&quot;,&quot;pelagic&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;ocean+&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Marine Ecoregions and Pelagic Provinces of the World (2007; 2012)&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-05-28T11:25:55.641+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/80567b4443f4457b822f645a2f0d70cf/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1655303802923.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Bailey R. G. 1989. Ecoregions: The Ecosystem Geography of Oceans and Continents. New York: Springer-Verlag.&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-10-03T14:50:28.484+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2011-10-10&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Download Dataset  The purpose of the work, which began in 1976, was to show how the nat...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;1d5d46888b1e4fb19c45042de1e576b2&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:834,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:false,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;Bailey&#39;s Ecoregions of the World (1989)&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;bailey&quot;,&quot;habitat&quot;,&quot;ecoregions&quot;,&quot;world&quot;,&quot;global&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Bailey&#39;s Ecoregions of the World (1989)&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-07-18T16:11:59.798+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/1d5d46888b1e4fb19c45042de1e576b2/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1664882649181.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;UNEP-WCMC, Short FT (2021). Global distribution of seagrasses (version 7.1). Seventh update to the data layer used in Green and Short (2003). Cambridge (UK): UN Environment Programme World Conservation Monitoring Centre. Data DOI: https://doi.org/10.34892/x6r3-d211&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-08T14:03:56.965+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2021-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Download Dataset \n\n\nThis dataset shows the global distribution of seagrasses, and is co...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;aaa46cd3d3d640b2916b8f0a0ffe07cb&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:13849,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;This dataset was originally developed alongside the publication by Green and Short (2003), and was the first authoritative and comprehensive global synthesis of the spatial distribution and status of seagrasses.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;Ocean+ Habitats&quot;,&quot;UNEP-WCMC&quot;,&quot;Global&quot;,&quot;Seagrasses&quot;,&quot;coastal&quot;,&quot;marine&quot;,&quot;blue carbon&quot;,&quot;seagrass&quot;,&quot;habitat&quot;,&quot;biogenic&quot;,&quot;ecosystem&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global Distribution of Seagrasses&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-05-28T11:10:42.922+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/aaa46cd3d3d640b2916b8f0a0ffe07cb/info/thumbnail/thumbnail.JPEG&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Fajardo, J., Bhattacharjee, A., Beard, S., Upton, J., Kamath, V., Dawkins, K., Telhado, C., and Baggaley, S.  (2023). Screening for restoration opportunities. A spatial layer to screen for opportunities to deliver multiple benefits through ecosystem restoration in Europe. UNEP-WCMC: Cambridge, UK.&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2023-04-21T08:14:25.662+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;-4712-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The business case for restoration is growing, and there is increasing evidence that the...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;a154e3e8fbbc4214a61a5b9f033cee0c&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by-sa&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:437,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;UNEP-WCMC has developed a spatial data layer to allow companies to screen for locations that offer opportunities to deliver multiple benefits through ecosystem restoration across Europe. The restoration opportunities layer is intended to be used alongside other data as part of screening and scoping exercises and should be validated on-ground as appropriate.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;Ecosystem restoration&quot;,&quot;Restoration&quot;,&quot;Restoration potential&quot;,&quot;Spatial planning&quot;,&quot;SCP&quot;,&quot;Nature&#39;s Contributions to People&quot;,&quot;Restoration opportunities&quot;,&quot;Europe&quot;,&quot;Proteus&quot;,&quot;Proteus Partners&quot;,&quot;Private sector&quot;,&quot;cc-by-sa&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Restoration Opportunities, Europe (2023)&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2023-05-04T12:00:34.061+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/a154e3e8fbbc4214a61a5b9f033cee0c/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1682066195616.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;UNEP-WCMC (2025) Global Critical Habitat screening layer (Version 2.1). Cambridge (UK): UN Environment Programme World Conservation Monitoring Centre. Data DOI: https://doi.org/10.34892/d3xm-qm60 . Other cited reference(s):UNEP-WCMC (2017) Global Critical Habitat screening layer (Version 1.0). Cambridge (UK): UN Environment Programme World Conservation Monitoring Centre. Data DOI:https://doi.org/10.34892/nc6d-0z73 .&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2025-04-04T10:12:18.911+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2025-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Download Dataset \n\nThe International Finance Corporation’s (IFC’s) Performance Standard...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;97a22bbe36c84895846a2bdc27cef8ba&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by-nc&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:523,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;The global Critical Habitat screening layer Version 2.1 has been developed to incorporate the latest versions of all input datasets, many of which have themselves been updated since Version 2.0 of the layer. It also includes some improvements and corrections in processing of the input data for great apes, cold water corals and cloud forests. The global Critical Habitat screening layer Version 2.0 was been developed since IFC have revised its guidance for determining Critical Habitat and global-scale biodiversity data have been updated and improved. The layer was developed to assess the likelihood of sites or operations being located within PS6-defined Critical Habitat in the early project screening stages.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;global&quot;,&quot;international-finance-corporation-performance-standard-6&quot;,&quot;biodiversity-safeguards&quot;,&quot;key-biodiversity-areas&quot;,&quot;-protected-areas&quot;,&quot;conservation&quot;,&quot;cc-by-nc&quot;,&quot;ocean+&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global Critical Habitat Screening Layer - Drill&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2025-10-03T09:49:45.922+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/97a22bbe36c84895846a2bdc27cef8ba/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1743772421572.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;UNEP-WCMC (2025) Global Critical Habitat screening layer (Version 2.1). Cambridge (UK): UN Environment Programme World Conservation Monitoring Centre. Data DOI: https://doi.org/10.34892/snwv-a025 . Other cited reference(s):UNEP-WCMC (2017) Global Critical Habitat screening layer (Version 1.0). Cambridge (UK): UN Environment Programme World Conservation Monitoring Centre. Data DOI: https://doi.org/10.34892/nc6d-0z73 .&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2023-12-05T11:44:43.690+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;-4712-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Download DatasetThe International Finance Corporation’s (IFC’s) Performance Standard 6 ...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;60c2f45412b4460ab17c2d8cd8bcc5f7&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:2593,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;The global Critical Habitat screening layer Version 2.1 has been developed to incorporate the latest versions of all input datasets, many of which have themselves been updated since Version 2.0 of the layer. It also includes some improvements and corrections in processing of the input data for great apes, cold water corals and cloud forests. The global Critical Habitat screening layer Version 2.0 was been developed since IFC have revised its guidance for determining Critical Habitat and global-scale biodiversity data have been updated and improved. The layer was developed to assess the likelihood of sites or operations being located within PS6-defined Critical Habitat in the early project screening stages.\nThe global Critical Habitat screening layer Version 1.0 was developed to assess the likelihood of sites or operations being located within PS6-defined Critical Habitat in the early project scoping phases.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;global&quot;,&quot;international-finance-corporation-performance-standard-6&quot;,&quot;biodiversity-safeguards&quot;,&quot;key-biodiversity-areas&quot;,&quot;-protected-areas&quot;,&quot;conservation&quot;,&quot;cc-by&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global Critical Habitat Screening Layer - Basic&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2025-10-03T09:50:45.576+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/60c2f45412b4460ab17c2d8cd8bcc5f7/info/thumbnail/ago_downloaded.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Citation: UNEP-WCMC. (2020). Human pressures on biodiversity, water and carbon. Cambridge, UK: UNEP-WCMC. https://doi.org/10.34892/ykjb-c787&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-08T14:03:26.021+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2021-02-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;In order to describe the human pressures on the biodiversity component of nature, we us...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;fabf96ab5e0c4becbd456ffc6f690113&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by-sa&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:971,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;The purpose of this dataset is to understand the spatial distribution of combined pressures on biodiversity, water provisioning services and carbon in the biomass and soils at a global scale. We selected a number of existing datasets which best represented pressures on these 3 components.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;Human pressures&quot;,&quot;cc-by-sa&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Human Pressures on biodiversity, water and carbon&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-06-21T12:31:25.349+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/fabf96ab5e0c4becbd456ffc6f690113/info/thumbnail/thumbnail.JPEG&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;WWF (2004) Simplified Biogeographical Realms of the World, generalised from  Olson, D.M., E. Dinerstein, E.D. Wikramanayake, N.D. Burgess, G.V.N. Powell, E.C. Underwood, J.A. D’Amico, H.E. Strand, J.C. Morrison, C.J. Loucks, T.F. Allnutt, J.F. Lamoreux, T.H. Ricketts, I. Itoua, W.W. Wettengel, Y. Kura, P. Hedao, and K. Kassem. (2001). Terrestrial ecoregions of the world: A new map of life on Earth. BioScience 51(11):933-938. DOI: 10.1641/0006-3568(2001)051[0933:TEOTWA]2.0.CO;2.&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-08T14:03:51.130+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2004-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Download Dataset \n\n\nThis map is a simplified representation of the eight Biogeographica...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;f196d94a226d430fa214947d51dad35a&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:4052,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:false,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;A global map of Biogeographical Realms of the world.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;world&quot;,&quot;Biogeographical Realm&quot;,&quot;Realm&quot;,&quot;biogeography&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Biogeographical Realms of the World (2004)&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2025-05-28T10:03:00.282+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/f196d94a226d430fa214947d51dad35a/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1656061498085.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;UNEP-WCMC and IUCN (2025), Protected Planet: The World Database on Protected Areas (WDPA)[On-line], [October 2025], Cambridge, UK: UNEP-WCMC and IUCN. Available at: https://doi.org/10.34892/6fwd-af11&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-16T09:31:21.520+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;-4712-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;\n                                The World Database of Protected Areas (WDPA) is the mo...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;1919c32890074ce5a589a1a99b48994b&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;wdpa&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:41664,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:false,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;The World Database on Protected Areas (WDPA) is the most comprehensive global database on terrestrial and marine protected areas. Version: October 2025. &quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;wdpa&quot;,&quot;protected-planet&quot;,&quot;wdpa&quot;,&quot;protected-areas&quot;,&quot;areas-of-biodiversity-importance&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;The World Database on Protected Areas&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2025-10-01T14:24:57.666+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/1919c32890074ce5a589a1a99b48994b/info/thumbnail/thumbnail.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2021-07-16T16:48:35.114+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;-4712-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Global spatially explicit characterization of 47 (version 001) terrestrial habitat type...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;79134b5187084c2499fc0b1b18e4c6d3&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:3483,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;The global habitat map is a spatial-explicit dataset produced through an intersection of best available data on land cover, climate and human pressures. The map follows the thematic legend of habitat classes as defined by the IUCN habitat classification system and maps as many terrestrial, freshwater and marine habitats as possible at global scale.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;IUCN habitat classification system&quot;,&quot;global&quot;,&quot;level 2&quot;,&quot;cc-by&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global Map of Terrestrial Habitat Types&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2023-01-24T11:52:18.183+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/79134b5187084c2499fc0b1b18e4c6d3/info/thumbnail/thumbnail.JPEG&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;Michael Hoffman, Kellee Koenig, Gill Bunting, Jennifer Costanza, \u0026 Williams, Kristen J. (2016). Biodiversity Hotspots (version 2016.1) (2016.1) [Data set]. Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3261807&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-23T08:52:41.272+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;2016-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;There are currently 36 recognized biodiversity hotspots. These are Earth’s most biologi...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;124b9a66d1c642b5bc41d1ff703a0d21&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;cc-by-sa&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:3281,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;Conservation International’s biodiversity hotspots—defined regions around the world where biodiversity conservation is most urgent because of high levels of endemism and human threat.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;Biodiversity Hotspots&quot;,&quot;Global&quot;,&quot;2011&quot;,&quot;cc-by-sa&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Biodiversity Hotspots (2016)&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2023-01-19T13:00:18.309+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/124b9a66d1c642b5bc41d1ff703a0d21/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1656664420044.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;UNEP-WCMC, WorldFish Centre, WRI, TNC (2021). Global distribution of coral reefs, compiled from multiple sources including the Millennium Coral Reef Mapping Project. Version 4.1, updated by UNEP-WCMC. Includes contributions from IMaRS-USF and IRD (2005), IMaRS-USF (2005) and Spalding et al. (2001). Cambridge (UK): UN Environment Programme World Conservation Monitoring Centre. Data DOI: https://doi.org/10.34892/t2wk-5t34&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-08T14:03:56.230+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;-4712-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Download Dataset \nThis dataset is the most comprehensive global dataset of warm-water c...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;0613604367334836863f5c0c10e452bf&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:23744,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;This dataset shows the global distribution of coral reefs in tropical and subtropical regions.&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;coral reefs&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc&quot;,&quot;portal&quot;,&quot;global&quot;,&quot;coastal&quot;,&quot;marine&quot;,&quot;habitats&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;ocean+&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global Distribution of Coral Reefs&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2024-05-28T12:04:21.434+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/0613604367334836863f5c0c10e452bf/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1677087907668.png&quot;},{&quot;avg_rating&quot;:0,&quot;citation&quot;:&quot;UNEP-WCMC (2001). Global Distribution of Dive Centres (ver 1.2). In supplement to: Spalding et al. (2001). Cambridge (UK): UN Environment World Conservation Monitoring Centre.&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2022-06-16T15:11:09.446+00:00&quot;,&quot;date_published&quot;:&quot;-4712-01-01&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;This dataset shows the global distribution of dive centres, some of which are PADI (Pro...&quot;,&quot;generic_image&quot;:false,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;21f96ee2103649b583d248f95f495eab&quot;,&quot;license&quot;:&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;,&quot;num_views&quot;:159,&quot;display_proteus_badge?&quot;:null,&quot;proteus?&quot;:true,&quot;proteus_exclusive?&quot;:false,&quot;resource_type&quot;:&quot;Geospatial Dataset&quot;,&quot;short_description&quot;:&quot;This dataset was created to accompany the World Atlas of Coral Reefs (map 2.1 in Spalding et al. 2001).&quot;,&quot;tags&quot;:[&quot;coastal&quot;,&quot;marine&quot;,&quot;human&quot;,&quot;unep-wcmc-general&quot;],&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Global Distribution of Dive Centres (2001)&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;GEOSPATIAL DATASET&quot;,&quot;updated_at&quot;:&quot;2023-01-24T12:04:44.075+00:00&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/sharing/rest/content/items/21f96ee2103649b583d248f95f495eab/info/thumbnail/thumbnail1655477436666.png&quot;}]"
